Nope, if you have neither telepathy nor active monster detection, the
message is:
A wave of psychic energy pours over you!  It locks on to your mind!

> However, I think that once you *do* have telepathy, the word latent
> should be dropped from the message.

The normal player intrinsic "telepathy" can be overridden by normal
vision and only kicks in once the character is blind; as long as the
intrinsic is /latent/, the game will take note of the fact that you're
not currently using your telepathy to observe creatures.

And yes, the game apparently counts multiple-turn monster detection as
a sort of telepathy, or it wouldn't word it like that.

> I also think non-telepaths should
> get some kind of advantage here- who says intrinsics shouldn't have a
> down-seide?

I'm not sure, but having a mind flayer lock onto your 'mind' may do
less damage than the blast locking onto your '(latent) telepathy'.

